[{"id": "387", "text": "revolut just launched a euro stablecoin on ethereum. EURR, pegged 1:1, issued by stripe-owned bridge under MiCA, live in denmark, poland and portugal first.\n\nevery euro stablecoin combined is worth about $810m. revolut holds $67.5bn of customer balances. if 1% of that moved into EURR it would be the biggest euro stablecoin on day one.\n\nthe timing is not a coincidence. MiCA forced USDT out of the EU app by end of august, and a regulated euro token lands the same month.", "photos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/ZXCcIcMxIN5wJ2XJjSnIGIgYElH_jakC2X13w_pufxZAdB3JJWknEBJpiWXOxNDHxNA0ye6p7ji2Qc0dzhOMajD6Y2auoOA6w4Eb-g11Deq3bcbsts-PBRAMaM8DjgGgyNLtFH2Rxu-mu7uZMOf0r-fDfV6rF4xc_muKOe9IekmFxSQ2nSUbJpmgTM6P-oMC8UF-5yD8uUwS2dTiBlzcnWZJM8tGIlWPHAUCJkzWHonVnLaq9nPZxqxxX7KCgGw_IfVKb5p6-o740VCu7G6GaxvTHYRB8dgj1WNhllPIlk4dG72T-NfiEOsQB4JWbkhYBzZI4XeFpCSRrjDnIWffvg.jpg"], "videos": []}, {"id": "385", "text": "so that ox-alpha model that topped openrouter last week turned out to be z.ai's GLM-5.3-Flash\n\n23.2 trillion tokens in 6 days, 2.3x the next model. biggest model in openrouter history and nobody knew whose it was\n\nnow it's official: 320B MoE with 18B active, first natively multimodal GLM-5, 1M context, MIT license. trained and served entirely on chinese chips\n\ncosts a tenth of GLM-5.2 and lands near opus 4.8 on coding and agentic benchmarks\n\nopen weights on huggingface, day one. at 18B active you can actually serve this thing yourself", "photos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/Z9mEiGtzPhhKUqbRidHyJ15BJofhfcdDaGbKPuhY8xCTfng2tQop72yHd3RrZd1TjtzQkFhv3XyZnnNWOhwCv2qmYTB7bLWCu4TIZZ6rCtVneCqFRrRi09KWM2lPUeWdetcB1oKi_UV2AgF7z9_UurO9es3AlKQIQPxdX-0bjyl8cyIsaoYke6tG_3wnN0N5dX9iP42BBVm3BPfB7mv957GEddjzH7bZWOW-ddWIqhCCp5y8mvs7MkigFqfy66nnpWuHL1_wK-qd5NbX6G0Ebimo5_8TtdPudcgsNTSn4R0rLTCzloUoRD4hbtOcFr90mL6A-0Y8IWAgINh2JBvV0w.jpg"], "videos": []}, {"id": "381", "text": "a coffee company made a game where you find one missing semicolon in 187,421 printed lines of code\n\nterminal.shop dropped semicolon inspector. first-person browser game where the entire codebase is printed out and taped to the walls of an office. you walk around with a magnifying glass and inspect sheets line by line.\n\nthe code on the walls is fake enterprise code with comments like \"revert after demo\", \"prod is different\", \"works on my machine\". one drawer is labeled DO NOT TOUCH THIS and it's empty.\n\nthere are achievements for the things you'd try instead of actually reading. none of them work.\n\nfree to play. WASD to move, scroll to zoom, click a line to accuse it.", "photos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/Y0GDzsSygPjRxibX4IMfdscw56Vt5G3h0dpJOhmv-gFbbSsJMVN1Qty6h1PhYRqrLFgFDegEIsR92zaeWuWildm_TLIFzUdOjCLGu1YNSdvAYdd-kzcP_V-OzHP7XL8ThXGqFYzX5530IMoSc6d4MmJ6xxP4Hqbfse-n-GgDZHVRsH756VumP5o02AKKZYka7MUkgMJt9ox3Gsa2zw1YPr5EJSxz5Zp-tvT1NAYOjfTwqtlYFZMPAqSPbraUpoZ_DgWemcHPhQsS5oORbqNte3Cl6s-OvNQiz77QgAj7cX2q6R3lB2_hw7NHITAxnsOg0FKZsyMMSuT0ySqJF2RfcQ"], "videos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/9977e0efb9.mp4?token=Ie05fVwPwQz_Ktl2Y417EKKBHf1RSGYDvGqkXnRNYQMovxGPmTDwJfM4wh8l-A0tDLeDmf3i1p_U66Dr0ZXcKWa6YkT_1DwL2ewwvDBm2erGsj6pi1AxHRviqYIDKvNGe0esh9WtNe4n9G6PDxqffQdy3IGWVJxacn62MlArD7qnKkPg26RSKnTuoCL6nknM-nYgsCCfpIsg6Ud_dthvTNjhFCIuNAUIC0JO3hq5Kn96yW2BDhG-NcqyTZiLc4SJWfCdvEudULHPkwaPVXGAWdooYGcwH3hM0za-3VBvY4tT61mc7xbRnIXbK2c0j9DhapZRcc39coqKlkYm71_xxw"]}, {"id": "380", "text": "browsers might soon verify your email for you\n\nno more \"check your inbox.\" resend wrote up the email verification api, a new browser proposal that confirms you own an address without ever leaving the signup form.\n\nthe flow: you're logged into gmail in chrome. you type your email into a form. the browser and your mailbox provider silently mint a token into a hidden field. your server verifies the token. done, no otp, no magic link.\n\nthat inbox detour is where signups go to die, so this kills the worst step of the double opt-in flow. fewer mistyped addresses too, which means fewer bounces and a cleaner sender reputation.\n\nthe catch: it's early. chrome only, via origin trial, and gmail is the only mailbox that supports it. usable today as a progressive enhancement, with a classic otp fallback everywhere else.\n\nresend shipped an npm package (email-verification-api) that handles the token verification server side, plus a full next.js example app you can try live.", "photos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/f93fzZB7QiRmQilKapo4gGi0PMSC4SaSljxsvn4S4VagPV-ND6MNR_3Q1NK1W5FQIfGoHBByfCAMTFKwIparG9IFnI3KlCMuoOAUri-VA27IS4BQmduqimJcHpHGGLWIWaIg32p2DF4iMTO8wjCQy--4mt4fIHgkilaeBW-eBuNyWXE3WrSZJiOchqi89S9kbqfhpLAXkqZxpalXaFABGWAcnZm5HP5UlEUBMLKXAtqolxjNhfeH1BNfJqMnP_ueTeL_7m5xoGH_sL6pK1UOlQde0JOUy1_72dddif_LieNISvx-msRKJYZUb2FKLyR9L-8Pwac6hSDczx_rnjyJQg"], "videos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/ac92897979.mp4?token=VPT4KkARc1bmHIU0exB_FfPILf1GvG_Q_bQR8fK9O_BuWvIqDmUoAOWaNSSA1Ce9GinTx5ejdweT1sQnYw9qUSgkZi_RF65PNd_hbHf6nefJEO-wQMDvrOuIvWXqCcYnzRUW80G-eiM0xGpXT95R07WpI_AISIwH3egfZ3QCzhSCEt0KDTwZb7xfjXoRfEEmG6_pUEaI-ynXDGF3Hx9R5BVHY8Eyui24GG0-ykXlhUhAyG8acJHkKPwqRCpjD2aD1elcNRaej1cOjRHT5xJnas1J0_iHhE2NugmeXi0vJPpmQxqaStYfdBYRvYdGH1LzUp9y4f2vJ-uZRHeZz9PYAQ"]}, {"id": "376", "text": "Multiple patients at a Nashville hospital are paralyzed after staff accidentally gave them the wrong drugs.\n\nThe hospital says they are \"sorry\" after injecting potassium chloride into the spines of people getting routine joint replacement surgeries.\n\nHospital staff noticed something was off when multiple patients went into cardiac arrest.", "photos": [], "videos": []}, {"id": "369", "text": "cursor just launched origin, their own code hosting platform\n\nrepos, pull requests, code browsing, github sync. prs sync both ways. comment in cursor, it shows up on github. review and merge without leaving the editor.\n\nvercel, buildkite, and depot integrations are live at launch. beta rolls out to all paid plans today.\n\nand they shipped it the same day github went down with a critical incident. best launch timing of the year, accidentally.", "photos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/hPw4AElyS_El8K9I29eh8V_iPBVVfDgytZrFRTigcuWmbISYZmk-aCUjJuAujtEhIDjMjVosI6tL906aeD3RpXRK6dE0vyJuRMhwYm4VcdIN0DWW5jS0sq1gnzp90zEshG1O27fAcE3qH1fM1LBlpxStWeS0Z7Hz8TlRIw_QZBXUJ25w5nhlfpAKxDrm7JVokeaKmkksZk_RcFAMOa-qSXf9cGDpgTOGxk8_b0_pDgUg_gs0yoj0JW44FAAiSVEX1KwklvCeXOlyZqcSUVHfAjpPW6SYiZ4fEMW2U54ZxGPGMFeK28k2p0tbmyxG8fOh1Qm4W94GdBQjo1gNJ2mTQw"], "videos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/f940b3af8c.mp4?token=Gan-pC_updmtqzdM9dzwzEXSkWgh0vQE_oza6krUsCo5gXX8cqiEpl-9eIKqsev7iqHCSHYuA0zlyzmtvLvbSCQ1y7fK2-kGD37i7s7SKmqmVL6S7nguawA-8yhm84ob7SF3jfaE9UWi3OKAzoeirO9cbnM-A-RHF6EDnr00RujiLwx5X5IjegJjTBZlvL3I3nztu6nOHU7baM_jNRwbI_V5mRVsH8TZScT3xT1BsKeabGfnE9X0vU0lztLUxDh8Casb8pukkQJcbho2XVZ7Gfr7OzfUrWW9_TPMI3ZoK8w92xNegDXSO-ne58TU9ir0GMDNP4TKBPrZNpmknO73Og"]}, {"id": "367", "text": "stripe is buying openrouter for $7b+\n\nbloomberg reports the deal is finalized. openrouter was valued at $1.3b just 82 days ago.\n\nthats a 5.4x jump in under three months.\n\nopenrouter is the one api that lets companies switch between 400+ ai models. 8 million users. they call it \"stripe for ai\" because it prevents lock-in and handles all the billing.\n\nnow stripe owns the actual stripe for ai.", "photos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/Q9vI0P63_kRRCo3ee4X5_pcqVz4aqYb0_4T2SjhhE5kV-pmeD3CK_8A1qMV0pT6KeJygyc5w0Kgzm1ewxJepLdzP0w7UKt6vYtI_uLouFGbjh26wy3EbrQEYVoViFMgC-K42d2g8Fs0G1JQiAafoaGOB4FtUm793PrvsKq7MbFPTk1Pgzf9hi6Oqxh_Xd3ceqdVx1twUflYZ9CRmta8_4Xc9dBPvuhZZ6KDdRSFngQuz72txYfp8W6c6P4eeXMgZOcCs7iy127tCRKXgC16U4_frM9ey9SNaDNfJdq8I5r7R04L4zpB0han5G0VkS66fWPoS7uqySc90TR0Ak4RwPA.jpg"], "videos": []}, {"id": "79", "text": "skoda duobell\n\nthe first bike bell designed to penetrate noise cancelling headphones\n\nskoda found the one frequency ANC can't fully block (750hz) and built a mechanical bell around it with a second frequency for extra reliability. tested in london, heard 22 meters earlier than a standard bell. analog solution to a digital problem\n\nhttps://youtu.be/zDaVPfpQvPI", "photos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/IFU4zEoXmFVe6V1uHiP3bDoy-XzZRz7AEfEWNvHXhiM6omwIlSBU2Cl74P-KplwJyD_vtdO9dzctPvOuVL_yTms95gvSaHZpNybzZz5Bv6-uX3iewEZvbcwuu_1XTNMuJMydlCtc62QnUNJDXvgasX8v6z5boRATG0jfQuoQ3Vz9rl7hu7VR4S9_-y0UoMx3M3QtZEDpzylVk2EdI2V97sGyQmjr3G58BlNOuqTNLKf_4we0TQLBgMs8hjaq29nNrZzTWWwVM5xXo4TAegnCOZwB4OnkhkoXF9fIL2x42H4JWLGGY36piGDByg7xnRL2WII8HTqB_DgDSFwEX_opeA"], "videos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/10b29ad1aa.mp4?token=RZH2hJuy6b_CcS6SQOTfbokB3mPHruEyTgw8whlbsmVMCxXTM4Cl4rs9hvv2XHpChN53g8ijSXWCBb1WTKcCJjtQ4JutbxGP9trTKsbLVLx89478v5Amz2ptDL_ZRsDCiR7khsa336OaLU0q5hZLsULTZcn3iGeYxDo_v1Zu1yRiMHOtbZeffDp5sctQdFg8c-ga4kYp9OLLMi3glVNLz9Sm6yJ25ehZggk2XryGW7xrQm0jWBLMJerFQka3MABdxj93U0UEHGNAdjNZx11dKchaWdd-Cz4ePq1jVcHWYLHIQh7seCfTxq21UjkCd8nl02aqKwxvjZwnqB-OsaEzWCBDQ6yljVsn_4BowIWnyoVU3A2mD9M5zNHCRtx9U5y_5_EcHvHp-iJwnFMORSBsCGO4IUoIWZG9OITSY-8z-vBuXT43whq0xzECYpgAqQQFTTpS22JOMrF5wAdKNSXsVb4LgOI3e1xtMjq2nSyJcd6HfjpA6O0ZyGDCsCu5YFGUIIYG3hDIw0vpbsTh33SDZTO64rSEu6UkQCLnNTvBYk9luykbtkqH8EqJrsLuxZ4OE6gziCFwyrWNGOMsbiymGmO9Ia1PxPGvTiFSjb36Gjnz_30X5jrc9upV1G3Z-RVkuxzWZHv8YpnVjrtJ2GQGh61lUDNHlMfbEPZYTCU5VS0"]}, {"id": "78", "text": "trump says the current financial system is outdated and plans to replace it with a cryptocurrency framework under the new structure bill.", "photos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/gtl9b1tsOqRjd5lBGyOY_NLGBY0BpXxvapGpw-qe6f3FawlqYENFtjvAi9R4kJ8P4mH8yLVPptMcFJF4MI3EWAObvFJJszqIicRSncsmqPagMigxd3Pg8U1yPALI4GuL8Eak83QnH7G8mslMyEW_NAkuuS6_E8CS9uZYbJ00ULYEgO5G7i4WNArcn7BpoR6Y7__t4B7wNpNwc8HSU2S5J8JYCJgHCOHXnmAjQI1-m0pDVCMrptieTC5yg-UqPZo54mzUsNWt8ZQdas4zHmZMZOAfoiOa6G8bf1-JyAJ4rl-zgT0gvHgeQ5znPLAa7anWqlVJLcTyWSoYQ1pXzSH1NQ"], "videos": ["https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/37a4cde184.mp4?token=cgTmNkpJg0RvqlhuRRLHp0um9eeJC374PebhxScJiuLoOpLqcGTjU3ky36nfnzis2ANnCaENSHdheXBTEDWzz-zoR8iffhFTa7KhnOQznz-pUzVJ6MCJ_5S3NguhJzgl12h1Yka9vxowFp1RLb